Mike Rockwell "continues to seriously consider stepping down" as Apple's vice president of Siri engineering and could leave the company altogether next year, according to <a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/newsletters/2026-11-08/apple-explores-turning-siri-ai-into-chatgpt-dots-like-agent-ios-28-shake-up"><em>Bloomberg</em>'s Mark Gurman</a>. Gurman described the potential move as a major blow to Apple.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2024/06/craig-federighi.jpg" alt="" width="1280" height="721" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-953979" /><br/>
If Rockwell departs or moves to another role, responsibility for Siri would likely fall to one of two people. Amar Subramanya is a Google veteran hired last year to shore up Apple's AI efforts, and Sebastien Marineau, a deputy to software chief Craig Federighi, leads the teams integrating AI into iOS. Marineau is said to be seen by some inside Apple as a possible eventual successor to Federighi himself, and as someone "more all-in on the AI revolution."<br/>
<br/>
As for Rockwell, he created the Vision Pro, before being put in charge of Siri's turnaround, but only after "an embarrassing two-year delay," as Gurman puts it. <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/22/vision-pro-creator-considered-leaving-apple/">Reports of him weighing an exit from Apple first surfaced in April</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Hair Force One, however, isn't going anywhere, it seems. A succession to Federighi remains "a distant prospect," reckons Gurman. Federighi "maintains a firm grip" on Apple's software engineering organization and "has done little to prioritize succession planning or establish a clear path for a successor," according to his sources. Gurman adds that Federighi, who has led the organization for more than a decade, has given no indication that he is among Apple's senior leaders considering an exit in the coming years.<div class="linkback">Tags: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mark-gurman/">Mark Gurman</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri-ai/">Siri AI</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/09/apple-siri-boss-may-leave/">Apple&#039;s Siri Boss May Leave - Here&#039;s Who Could Take Over</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/apples-siri-boss-may-leave-heres-who-could-take-over.2493986/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>